# Browser → OpenWA API.
# Leave VITE_OPENWA_URL empty for same-origin (`/api` + `/socket.io`):
#   - `npm run dev` — UI on :2785 (Vite proxies `/api` and `/socket.io` to Nest on :2786)
#   - production image — Nest serves UI and `/api` on :2785
# Split-origin deploys can still pin the API origin at build time:
# VITE_OPENWA_URL=https://api.example.com
# VITE_OPENWA_APIKEY=your_api_key_here

# Railway / Node server (frontend-only deploy): Nitro must use node-server, not vercel.
# railway.json sets NITRO_PRESET on build; do not run `npm ci` again in buildCommand — Railpack
# already ran `npm install` (see frontend/.npmrc keeps devDependencies for Vite).
#
# Server-side proxy (`/api/auth/validate`, `/api/whatsapp`, …) when UI and API are separate:
# WA_GATEWAY_URL=https://your-openwa-api.up.railway.app
#
# API must allow this UI origin in CORS_ORIGINS when the browser calls the API directly
# (not needed when same-origin / Vite proxy is used):
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.example.com
